---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const psy = await getCollection('en_psychology');
const bio = await getCollection('en_biology');
const all = [...psy.map((p) => ({...p, cat: 'psychology' as const})), ...bio.map((p) => ({...p, cat: 'biology' as const}))];
const relatedTags = ['sleep', 'circadian', 'brain', 'memory'];
const related = all
  .filter((p) => (p.data.tags ?? []).some((t) => relatedTags.includes(t)))
  .sort((a, b) => (a.data.generated_at < b.data.generated_at ? 1 : -1));

export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Sleep Science: An Evidence Hub — Deprivation, Circadian Rhythm, Memory｜PubMed Trivia"
  description="How sleep deprivation affects cognition, metabolism, and mental health; circadian rhythm biology; sleep and memory consolidation. Curated from systematic reviews."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="hub">
    <header class="hub__header">
      <p class="hub__breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">Home</a> › 😴 Sleep Hub</p>
      <h1>😴 Sleep Science: An Evidence Hub</h1>
      <p class="hub__lede">
        Sleep is a foundational biological process affecting <strong>cognition, mood, metabolism, and immunity</strong>.
        Modern industrialized societies increasingly sleep less than the biological requirement, with measurable
        consequences at the population level. This hub curates our systematic-review-based articles on sleep science.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="hub__toc" aria-label="Contents">
      <p class="hub__toc-title">Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#basics">Sleep architecture</a></li>
        <li><a href="#deprivation">Effects of sleep deprivation</a></li>
        <li><a href="#circadian">Circadian rhythm and the body clock</a></li>
        <li><a href="#memory">Sleep and memory consolidation</a></li>
        <li><a href="#practical">Practical steps for better sleep</a></li>
        <li><a href="#learn-more">Learn more</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <section id="basics">
      <h2>1. Sleep architecture</h2>
      <p>
        A normal night cycles between <strong>non-REM (stages 1-3)</strong> and <strong>REM sleep</strong> about every 90 minutes.
        Deep non-REM (stage 3) supports physical restoration, memory consolidation, and immune function.
        REM contributes to emotional processing, creativity, and memory integration.
      </p>
      <p>
        Typical adults complete 4-6 cycles per night, with REM percentage increasing toward morning.
        This is why we tend to wake more easily during the last third of sleep.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="deprivation">
      <h2>2. Effects of sleep deprivation</h2>
      <p>
        A single night of <strong>total sleep deprivation</strong> produces cognitive impairment equivalent to
        a blood alcohol level of ~0.10%. Chronic short sleep (&lt;6 hours nightly) is associated with elevated risk of
        <strong>obesity, type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and dementia</strong> in large cohort studies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="circadian">
      <h2>3. Circadian rhythm and the body clock</h2>
      <p>
        The suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN) in the hypothalamus runs a <strong>~24.2-hour cycle</strong>, resetting daily
        via morning light exposure. Bright evening light — especially blue wavelengths — suppresses melatonin secretion
        and delays sleep onset.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="memory">
      <h2>4. Sleep and memory consolidation</h2>
      <p>
        Newly acquired information is transferred from the hippocampus to the neocortex during sleep, particularly
        during slow-wave sleep. This is why <em>all-nighter</em> study strategies underperform distributed practice
        with normal sleep. Even a <strong>short nap (10-30 min)</strong> can enhance memory consolidation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="practical">
      <h2>5. Practical steps for better sleep</h2>
      <div class="hub__grid">
        <div class="hub__card">
          <h4>☀️ Morning light exposure</h4>
          <p>15 min of &gt;2,000 lux within 30 min of waking. Outdoor walk is ideal.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hub__card">
          <h4>🌙 Evening light management</h4>
          <p>Reduce bright light and blue wavelengths 2 hours before bed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hub__card">
          <h4>☕ Caffeine timing</h4>
          <p>Caffeine half-life is 5-7 hours. Avoid after ~2 pm for most people.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hub__card">
          <h4>🍽️ Meal timing</h4>
          <p>Finish eating 3 hours before bedtime. Fat and alcohol especially disrupt sleep architecture.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p><strong>Related articles (latest):</strong></p>
    <ul class="hub__link-list">
      {related.slice(0, 10).map((p) => (
        <li><a href={`/en/${p.cat}/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <section id="learn-more">
      <h2>6. Learn more</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/lab/">🔬 PubMed Lab — search papers + chat with AI</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/editorial-policy/">📝 Editorial policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/tag/sleep/">🏷️ #sleep tag</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/tag/circadian/">🏷️ #circadian tag</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="hub__updated">Last updated: 2026-09-24</p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .hub { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 20px 48px; }
    .hub__breadcrumb { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .hub__breadcrumb a { color: var(--muted); }
    .hub__header h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 8px 0 16px; line-height: 1.4; }
    .hub__lede { line-height: 1.85; margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .hub__toc { background: #f7f9fc; border-left: 4px solid var(--navy); padding: 14px 18px 14px 22px; margin: 28px 0; border-radius: 4px; }
    .hub__toc-title { font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .hub__toc ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.85; }
    .hub__toc a { color: var(--link); }
    .hub h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 40px 0 16px; padding-left: 12px; border-left: 5px solid var(--navy); scroll-margin-top: 16px; }
    .hub h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 20px 0 8px; }
    .hub h4 { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 6px; }
    .hub p { line-height: 1.85; margin: 12px 0; }
    .hub ul, .hub ol { line-height: 1.9; }
    .hub__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin: 16px 0; }
    .hub__card { background: white; border: 1px solid #e5e9f2; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; }
    .hub__card p { margin: 4px 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .hub__link-list { padding-left: 24px; }
    .hub__link-list li { margin: 6px 0; }
    .hub__link-list a { color: var(--link); }
    .hub__updated { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; text-align: center; margin-top: 36px; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
